      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "i could see this making more sense for allowing the option to turn your home world into a friends only world without making a new instance of your home world. Allow only those users who know you from your friends list to join. However, I'd probably hold on the friends+ function only because, despite the fact that your friend is with you, you may or may not know who their friend(s) is.\nSay that you want to have your friend join your home world and you either just wanna chill and watch movies/YouTube videos on your home's video player (depending on what your home world is). But then one of their friends joins off them, and let's say that they're some person that likes to annoy others (cause there can be some friends that are like that). Keep in mind that this is your friend's friend. While yes you can kick that person out of your home world depending on if they're being annoying/intrusive, it's an unnecessary step for you to take and is about a minute of your time taken.\nWhile I'm not saying that a friends+ home world isn't possible, it's simply that I would rather want it to be a home world where I can allow anyone of my online friends, who I'm most familiar with, to join without having to send an invite request all the time.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
